     2| * IVX durable document store (Supabase-backed) — THE PERMANENT DATA-LOSS FIX (2026-06-07).
     3| *
     4| * Why this exists:
     5| *   The Render web service runs on a tier WITHOUT a persistent disk, so every IVX
     6| *   business store (leads, CRM, deals, outreach, capital pipeline) that wrote JSON
     7| *   files to the local filesystem was wiped on every deploy/restart — deals 3 → 0,
     8| *   CRM → 0, leads reset. A mounted disk requires a paid Render plan + payment method
     9| *   that isn't available, so the filesystem can never be durable here.
    10| *
    11| *   This module persists each store's JSON state into Supabase Postgres (the same
    12| *   database the public chat already uses durably), keyed by the store's file path.
    13| *   Data now survives restarts, deploys, and tier changes regardless of disk.
    14| *
    15| * Design:
    16| *   - One table `ivx_durable_documents(doc_key text pk, value jsonb, updated_at)`
    17| *     holds the materialised state for each store (one row per JSON file).
    18| *   - One table `ivx_durable_events(id bigserial, doc_key, event jsonb, created_at)`
    19| *     holds the append-only forensic event log (replaces the *.jsonl files).
    20| *   - Schema is created lazily and idempotently via the existing `ivx_exec_sql` RPC.
    21| *   - When Supabase is NOT configured (local dev / tests), callers fall back to the
    22| *     filesystem — see `isDurableStoreConfigured()`.
    23| */
